---
description: Backend rules for URL creation + redirect correctness
globs: ["backend/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

## Backend API shape (must match frontend)
- POST /api/links
- GET  /api/links?query=&tag_id=&status=&limit=&offset=
- POST /api/links/{code}/disable
- GET  /api/tags
- GET  /{code}  (redirect)

## Code generation
- CODE alphabet: A-Z a-z 0-9 (62 chars), fixed length (default 7 or 8).
- Use cryptographically secure RNG.
- Generate -> reject if reserved -> attempt INSERT -> on unique violation retry.
- Enforce DB unique index on code. Never rely solely on in-memory checks.

## Validation
- original_url must be a valid absolute URL.
- Default: allow only https:// (allow http:// only if explicitly enabled via config).
- expires_at must be NULL (permanent) or > now at creation time.
- tag is required.

## Status
- status in {active, disabled, blocked}. Expired can be derived from expires_at, but you may also expose it as computed field in responses.
- Never delete rows.

## Redirect
- On GET /{code}: fetch by code, check disabled/blocked/expired, then redirect.
- Use 302 by default.
- Do not log full URLs in error logs at high verbosity (avoid leaking sensitive query params).
